{"id": "30c9a43f-1a44-4cc0-96bf-8fe455f1750a", "timestamp": "2026-06-02T11:28:59.783503", "source": "agent", "thought": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "The generated Lexer.fs does NOT have `open Parser` at the top! The Lexer.fsl has `open Parser` but the generated code doesn't include it. This is because FsLex doesn't preserve `open` statements from the .fsl file header.\n\nThe fix is to either:\n1. Add `open Parser` to the generated Lexer.fs after generation\n2. Or use fully qualified names in the Lexer.fsl\n\nLet me update the Lexer.fsl to use fully qualified names, and also update the FixLineDirectives target to add `open Parser` to the generated Lexer.fs:\n\n"}], "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "python3 -c \"\ncontent = '''rule tokenize =\n    parse\n    | [' ' '\\\\t' '\\\\r' '\\\\n']\n        { tokenize lexbuf }\n    | ['0'-'9']+\n        { Parser.INT (int (lexeme_string lexbuf)) }\n    | '+'\n        { Parser.PLUS }\n    | '-'\n        { Parser.MINUS }\n    | '*'\n        { Parser.STAR }\n    | '/'\n        { Parser.SLASH }\n    | '('\n        { Parser.LPAREN }\n    | ')'\n        { Parser.RPAREN }\n    | eof\n        { Parser.EOF }\n    | _\n        { failwith \\\"Unexpected character\\\" }\n'''\nwith open('/Users/ohama/projs/OpenHandsTests/oh-workdir-planning/arm-a/fsharp-r2/calc/Lexer.fsl', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(content)\nprint('Written successfully')\n\"", "is_input": false, "timeout": null, "reset": false, "kind": "TerminalAction"}, "tool_name": "terminal", "tool_call_id": "b1451c02-0673-419c-94ec-49f4c18ae9ee", "tool_call": {"id": "b1451c02-0673-419c-94ec-49f4c18ae9ee", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "terminal", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"python3 -c \\\"\\ncontent = '''rule tokenize =\\n    parse\\n    | [' ' '\\\\\\\\t' '\\\\\\\\r' '\\\\\\\\n']\\n        { tokenize lexbuf }\\n    | ['0'-'9']+\\n        { Parser.INT (int (lexeme_string lexbuf)) }\\n    |