{"id": "c4ae7222-23d0-409a-b166-4303d540264f", "timestamp": "2026-06-02T11:32:56.119585", "source": "agent", "thought": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Now the issue is that `BeforeTargets=\"CoreCompile\"` means my target runs before CoreCompile, but the CallFsLex/CallFsYacc targets also run before CoreCompile. The order between them is not guaranteed. I need to ensure my target runs AFTER CallFsLex/CallFsYacc. Let me use a different approach - I'll add the sed commands to the CallFsLex/CallFsYacc targets by creating a custom targets file:\n\n"}], "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"thought": "The problem is that my FixLineDirectives target runs before CoreCompile, but CallFsLex/CallFsYacc also run before CoreCompile. The order between them is not guaranteed, so my sed commands might run before the files are generated.\n\nI need to ensure my target runs AFTER CallFsLex and CallFsYacc. Since these targets are defined in the package's targets file (not in my project), I can't use AfterTargets to reference them from my project.\n\nOne approach: I can override the CallFsLex and CallFsYacc targets by defining them in my project with the same name. MSBuild will use the project's definition. But that's complex.\n\nAnother approach: I can use DependsOnTargets in my target to depend on CallFsLex and CallFsYacc. But again, these are in a different project.\n\nActually, looking at the diag output more carefully:\n- The targets file IS imported (we see \"Property reassignment: $(CompileDependsOn)=\"CallFsLex;CallFsYacc;...\")\n- But the AfterTargets attribute in my project says the targets don't exist\n\nThis is because AfterTargets looks for targets in the current project, not in imported projects.\n\nThe simplest solution: I should use `DependsOnTargets=\"CallFsLex;CallFsYacc\"` in my target definition. This should work because MSBuild resolves targets from all imported projects.\n\nWait, actually let me re-read the error: \"The target 'CallFsLex' listed in an AfterTargets attribute... does not exist in the project, and will be ignored.\"\n\nThis means AfterTargets is ignored, so my target just runs BeforeTargets=\"CoreCompile\" without any ordering relative to CallFsLex/CallFsYacc.\n\nLet me try using DependsOnTargets instead:\n\n```xml\n<Target Name=\"FixLineDirectives\" DependsOnTargets=\"CallFsLex;CallFsYacc\" BeforeTargets=\"CoreCompile\">\n```\n\nThis should ensure CallFsLex and CallFsYacc run first, then my target runs.\n", "kind": "ThinkAction"}, "tool_name": "think", "tool_call_id": "ede3372c-529b-4dd4-9258-e0f987dad64a", "tool_call": {"id": "ede3372c-529b-4dd4-9258-e0f987dad64a", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "think", "arguments": "{\"thought\": \"The problem is that my FixLineDirectives target runs before CoreCompile, but CallFsLex/CallFsYacc also run before CoreCompile. The order between them is not guaranteed, so my sed commands might run before the files are generated.\\n\\nI need to ensure my target runs AFTER CallFsLex and CallFsYacc. Since these targets are defined in the package's targets file (not in my project), I can't use AfterTargets to reference them from my project.\\n\\nOne approach: I can override the CallFsLex and CallFsYacc targets by defining them in my project with the same name. MSBuild will use the project's definition. But that's complex.\\n\\nAnother approach: I can use DependsOnTargets in my target to depend on CallFsLex and CallFsYacc. But again, these are in a different project.\\n\\nActually, looking at the diag output more carefully:\\n- The targets file IS imported (we see \\\"Property reassignment: $(CompileDependsOn)=\\\"CallFsLex;CallFsYacc;...\\\")\\n- But the AfterTargets attribute in my project says the targets don't exist\\n\\nThis is because AfterTargets looks for targets in the current project, not in imported projects.\\n\\nThe simplest solution: I should use `DependsOnTargets=\\\"CallFsLex;CallFsYacc\\\"` in my target definition. This should work because MSBuild resolves targets from all imported projects.\\n\\nWait, actually let me re-read the error: \\\"The target 'CallFsLex' listed in an AfterTargets attribute... does not exist in the project, and will be ignored.\\\"\\n\\nThis means AfterTargets is ignored, so my target just runs BeforeTargets=\\\"CoreCompile\\\" without any ordering relative to CallFsLex/CallFsYacc.\\n\\nLet me try using DependsOnTargets instead:\\n\\n```xml\\n<Target Name=\\\"FixLineDirectives\\\" DependsOnTargets=\\\"CallFsLex;CallFsYacc\\\" BeforeTargets=\\\"CoreCompile\\\">\\n```\\n\\nThis should ensure CallFsLex and CallFsYacc run first, then my target runs.\\n\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-1d12af86-0c5e-4e03-9e43-34ef36ed1e3b", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "think: {\"thought\": \"The problem is that my FixLineDirectives target runs before CoreCompile, but CallFsLex/CallFsYacc also run before CoreCompile. The order between them is not guaranteed, so my sed commands might run before the files are generated.\\n\\nI need to ensure my target runs AFTER CallFsLex and CallFsYacc. Since these targets are defined in the package's targets file (not in my project), I can't use AfterTargets to reference them from my project.\\n\\nOne approach: I can override the CallFsLex and CallFsYacc targets by defining them in my project with the same name. MSBuild will use the project's definition. But that's complex.\\n\\nAnother approach: I can use DependsOnTargets in my target to depend on CallFsLex and CallFsYacc. But again, these are in a different project.\\n\\nActually, looking at the diag output more carefully:\\n- The targets file IS imported (we see \\\"Property reassignment: $(CompileDependsOn)=\\\"CallFsLex;CallFsYacc;...\\\")\\n- But the AfterTargets attribute in my project says the targets don't exist\\n\\nThis is because AfterTargets looks for targets in the current project, not in imported projects.\\n\\nThe simplest solution: I should use `DependsOnTargets=\\\"CallFsLex;CallFsYacc\\\"` in my target definition. This should work because MSBuild resolves targets from all imported projects.\\n\\nWait, actually let me re-read the error: \\\"The target 'CallFsLex' listed in an AfterTargets attribute... does not exist in the project, and will be ignored.\\\"\\n\\nThis means AfterTargets is ignored, so my target just runs BeforeTargets=\\\"CoreCompile\\\" without any ordering relative to CallFsLex/CallFsYacc.\\n\\nLet me try using DependsOnTargets instead:\\n\\n```xml\\n<Target Name=\\\"FixLineDirectives\\\" DependsOnTargets=\\\"CallFsLex;CallFsYacc\\\" BeforeTargets=\\\"CoreCompile\\\">\\n```\\n\\nThis should ensure CallFsLex and CallFsYacc run first, then my target runs.\\n\"}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
